<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply up $9.7 bln in Nov 4 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply up $9.7 bln in Nov 4 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $9.7 billion in the November 4 week to $3,791.3 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $12.0 billion to $4,841.2 billion. M-1 rose $300 million to $1,081.5 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,780.1 billion versus $3,774.1 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
